// GENERATED BY MATUGEN - do not edit by hand.
// Template: ~/.config/matugen/templates/niri-colors.kdl
// Wallpaper: {{image}}
//
// Included by ~/.config/niri/config.kdl, and it has to be included AFTER that
// file's own layout block. The order IS the mechanism, measured rather than
// assumed:
//
//   - `layout` is a singleton. Two of them in one file is a hard error --
//     "duplicate node `layout`, single node expected" from `niri validate`.
//     An include is the only way to have a second one at all.
//   - Included sections MERGE property by property, so naming active-gradient
//     here leaves width and inactive-color in config.kdl exactly as they are.
//     Nothing has to be repeated, and nothing goes stale when that file
//     changes.
//   - Includes are POSITIONAL: an include overrides what came before it and is
//     overridden by what comes after. Placed before the layout block this file
//     would be silently ignored, with the literals winning and the ring simply
//     never following the wallpaper.
//
// WITH the "#", unlike hypr-colors.lua. niri's colours are CSS colour strings,
// where a bare rrggbb is a parse error; Hyprland wants the naked hex because it
// wraps it in rgba(). Same two colours, opposite spelling -- which is why there
// are two templates and not one file shared between the flavors.
//
// The "ee" tail is alpha, ~93%, and it is here to match
// general.col.active_border in hyprland.lua, which is rgba(<hex>ee). Without it
// niri would draw the accent at full strength and the same wallpaper would look
// different in the two sessions.
//
// NO post_hook in config.toml for this template, and unlike most of the others
// that is not a limitation: niri watches the files it includes and reloads
// itself when one changes, so writing this file IS applying it. Hyprland needs
// `hyprctl eval` from wallpaper-switch for the same effect.
//
// primary and tertiary, the same pair and the same 45 degrees hypr-colors.lua
// feeds to accent and accent2.

layout {
    focus-ring {
        active-gradient from="{{colors.primary.default.hex}}ee" to="{{colors.tertiary.default.hex}}ee" angle=45
    }
}
